.TH "CITADEL" "1" "Sep 2026" "AceTeam" "Citadel CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
citadel-agents - Discover vendor coding agents installed on this node


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcitadel agents [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Detects vendor coding-agent CLIs already installed and authenticated on this
node, for the node's own account — not a container or binary AceTeam ships.

.PP
This is discovery only. It never spawns, drives, or runs a turn of any
vendor agent.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for agents


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug output

.PP
\fB--no-auto-update\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic update checks and installs for this run (or set CITADEL_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colorized output

.PP
\fB--node-dir\fP=""
	Override the node config directory (citadel.yaml + services/), bypassing $HOME/ConfigDir resolution. Also settable via CITADEL_NODE_DIR. Scope: manifest/services resolution only -- does NOT redirect network state, the module lockfile, or nodevault.

.PP
\fB--runtime\fP=""
	Container runtime for module containers: docker or podman (default: auto-detect)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcitadel(1)\fP, \fBcitadel-agents-probe(1)\fP
